# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the real values.
# .env.local is git-ignored — never commit real keys.
#
# All three come from the Supabase dashboard:
#   Project Settings → API

# Project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklm.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# "anon" / publishable key. Safe to expose to the browser: every request it
# makes is still constrained by Row Level Security.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# "service_role" / secret key. SERVER-ONLY — it bypasses Row Level Security.
# Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never import it into client code, and
# never paste it into the browser. Used only by server actions such as an admin
# creating a rep's login.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional. A contact string for the User-Agent the photo-stamp's area lookup
# sends to OpenStreetMap, whose usage policy asks for one — an email address or
# a URL. Leave it unset and the lookup still works; setting it is a courtesy to
# a free service we depend on for a convenience.
# PLACE_LOOKUP_CONTACT=you@example.com

# Optional. When set, /api/health returns a real database check to a caller
# that sends this value as the x-health-token header. The public response
# stays a static {"ok":true} either way — it must never touch the database,
# because anyone can poll it. Leave unset and the deep check does not exist.
HEALTH_CHECK_TOKEN=

# Optional. An Ola Maps API key for the photo stamp's area name. Set the
# client's own key here; if unset, the app uses free OpenStreetMap exactly as it
# always has — there is no degraded mode and no feature that stops working.
#
# WHAT IT CHANGES: only the NAME put on a set of coordinates, and only for the
# better in India, where Ola knows colonies and sectors OpenStreetMap often has
# as just a city. It does NOT change GPS accuracy — the position comes from the
# device and is untouched by any of this.
#
# SERVER-ONLY, and more pointedly than most: Ola takes the key as a QUERY
# PARAMETER, so a lookup made from the browser would hand it to anyone with the
# network tab open. No NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, never read from src/components, and
# on Cloudflare it goes in Secrets rather than build variables.
#
# One key, no client id, no secret, no token step. See docs/OLA-MAPS-SETUP.md
# for where to get it and how to verify it works.
# OLA_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional. The commit this bundle was built from, surfaced ONLY in the
# token-gated /api/health answer (never in the public {"ok":true}). It makes
# "has the new build gone out?" a one-line check, which matters because every
# screen that changes in the current rework sits behind auth — two consecutive
# builds are otherwise indistinguishable from outside.
#
# SET IT IN THE BUILD COMMAND, mapping the platform's own variable onto this
# generic name, so no platform spelling ever reaches src/:
#
#   Cloudflare Workers Builds:  APP_COMMIT_SHA=$WORKERS_CI_COMMIT_SHA npm run build
#   locally:                    APP_COMMIT_SHA=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD) npm run build
#
# NOT in wrangler.jsonc — that file must never grow a `vars` block, because
# Workers Builds prints plaintext vars into the build log. It is read at BUILD
# time: the OpenNext adapter bakes the build environment into the bundle, so no
# runtime binding is needed. Unset simply omits the field.
# APP_COMMIT_SHA=
